---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { clinic, formattedAddress } from '../data/clinic';

const lastUpdated = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-IN', {
  day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric',
});
---
<Base
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="How Sri Shankara Dental Clinic collects, uses and stores personal data submitted through this website, under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap-narrow prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This notice explains what personal data this website collects, why, and
        what you can do about it. It is written to meet the requirements of the
        Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023 and the DPDP Rules 2025.
      </p>

      <p><strong>Data fiduciary:</strong> {clinic.name}, {formattedAddress()}.</p>

      <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
      <p>
        This website collects personal data only when you choose to send it
        through the appointment request form. That is:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your name and phone number</strong> — so we can call you back to arrange an appointment.</li>
        <li><strong>Your email address</strong>, if you give it — as an alternative way to reach you, and to send the dental news email if you asked for it.</li>
        <li><strong>What you tell us in the message field</strong> — so we can prepare for your visit.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not use this data for any other purpose, and we do not sell it or
        share it for advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>Please do not send clinical details through this form</h2>
      <p>
        The form is for arranging appointments. Please do not include medical
        history, symptoms in detail, or images through it. Bring that to your
        appointment, or phone the clinic.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries that do not become appointments are deleted within
        24 months. Where you become a patient, your contact details
        become part of your clinical record and are retained in line with the
        clinic's records policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Who processes it</h2>
      <p>
        Form submissions are delivered to the clinic's email by Web3Forms. The
        dental news email, if you subscribe, is sent by Brevo. This site
        is hosted by Cloudflare. These providers process data on our
        instructions only.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the DPDP Act you may:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>ask what personal data of yours we hold and how it is being processed;</li>
        <li>ask us to correct or complete inaccurate data;</li>
        <li>ask us to erase your data, where we are not required to keep it;</li>
        <li>withdraw your consent at any time, as easily as you gave it;</li>
        <li>nominate another person to exercise these rights on your behalf;</li>
        <li>raise a grievance with us, and escalate to the Data Protection Board of India if it is not resolved.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Withdrawing consent</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${clinic.grievanceOfficer.email}`}>{clinic.grievanceOfficer.email}</a>
        and we will stop processing your data and delete it, unless we are
        required by law to retain it. To stop the news email, use the
        unsubscribe link at the foot of any issue.
      </p>

      <h2>Grievance officer</h2>
      <p>
        {clinic.grievanceOfficer.name === 'PLACEHOLDER'
          ? `The Practice Manager, ${clinic.name}`
          : clinic.grievanceOfficer.name}<br />
        <a href={`mailto:${clinic.grievanceOfficer.email}`}>{clinic.grievanceOfficer.email}</a>
      </p>
      <p>We aim to respond to any grievance within 30 days.</p>

      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no advertising or tracking cookies, and does not use
        third-party analytics. The only data that leaves your browser is what
        you choose to type into the appointment form.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>
        If this notice changes materially we will update the date below and,
        where required, contact you.
      </p>
      <p><em>Last updated: {lastUpdated}</em></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
